WEBVTT

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.710
I still have time to make it

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.710
Ima nara mada maniau kara

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.240
Better to withdraw now

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.240
Tettai shitahou ga iiyo

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:21.700
Before I misunderstand you even more

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:21.700
Motto kanchigai shite shimau maeni

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.790
The staple-words I fastened you with

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.790
Kimi wo tojita kotoba no hari

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:34.340
Somehow, now I find them piercing my heart...

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:34.340
Itsuno manika kono mune ni sasatte shimatteta

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.680
It hurts

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.680
Itai

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.970
It's all your fault

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.970
Kimi no sei dayo

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.680
Don't come near me, not when I'm like this

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.680
Konaide konna konna watashi wo

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.390
Don't look at me, not so deep into my heart

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.390
Minaide sonna sonna tokomade

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.650
Don't talk about it, not with that smile

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.650
Hanasanaide anna anna egao de

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.400
Not to anyone

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.400
Donna dare nimo

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.740
Going on forever,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.740
Dokomade demo tsuzuku

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.410
just like this sky

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.410
kono sora no you na

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.660
Please pledge never-ending eternity

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.660
Owari no nai eien wo chikatte

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.160
Both cruel and kind,

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.160
Ijiwaru de yasashii

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.830
just like that ocean

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.830
sono umi no youna

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.940
If I dive into your heart, please catch me

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.940
Kokoro ni tobikondara uketome te

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:17.220
These feelings can't be measured in weight

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:17.220
Omosa ja hakarenai konna omoi

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:23.870
And now I'm going to convey them only to you

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:23.870
Kimi dake ni ima tsutaeru kara

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.080
KOYOMI

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.080
STONE

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.080
KOYOMI

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.080
MONOGATARI

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.110
M

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.110
A

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.110
Y

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.100
M

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.100
A

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.100
Y

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.100
9

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.600
<i>Late Tuesday afternoon.</i>

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:49.210
<i>I was walking back from the cram school ruins with Senjougahara Hitagi.</i>

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.040
<i>She had been suffering.</i>

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:54.220
<i>She had been suffering so much,</i>

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.590
<i>she was numb to the pain.</i>

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.520
<i>And yesterday,</i>

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.620
<i>her battle against the illness finally came to an end.</i>

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:06.200
They say you know to appreciate health
when you recover from an illness.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.800
But since I was ill for so long,

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.520
just walking normally like this is a new sensation to me.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.770
Oh, I see.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.780
Now, how should I go about this?

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.280
About what?

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.230
Well, you know how Oshino-san billed me for this case, right?

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.790
Do you have savings or something?

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.070
No, I don't.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.640
I do have some debt, though.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.150
Senjougahara, do you know any ghost stories?

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:42.720
Oshino, as a specialist, primarily works on gathering apparition stories.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.030
If you have uncommon stories of apparitions,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.430
or rare urban legends...

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.430
If you know of stuff like that,

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.540
I thought you might be able to reduce that debt.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:52.960
Unfortunately,

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.070
I don't know any apparition stories that surpass what I experienced.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.550
Oh?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.140
What?

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.170
Don't get fresh.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:15.790
Oh, sorry.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.530
It's just that you were about to jump into the road.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.060
I wasn't going to jump.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.510
I just wanted to look at that.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.510
That?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:32.930
It looks like there was a traffic accident around here.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.450
Seems so.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.830
Something recent?

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.820
But if you got into an accident
because your focus was on those flowers,

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.210
the accident victim couldn't be at rest.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:43.450
You should be careful.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.830
I remember one now.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:48.710
Remember?

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.310
Remember what?

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.700
A "horror tale," Araragi-kun.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:53.940
What?

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:54.820
BLACK

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.850
This is an order from the princess.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.170
Do as you see fit.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.170
<i>Like there's a princess who talks like that.</i>

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.870
M

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.870
A

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.870
Y

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.870
10

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.370
<i>Following Senjougahara-hime's command,</i>

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:16.390
<i>I visited the rooftop of Naoetsu High School.</i>

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.700
It's true.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.650
It's just like Senjougahara said.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.130
<i>On the supposedly off-limits rooftop,</i>

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.360
<i>there was a brand new bouquet.</i>

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.400
How'd you get on the roof when it's off-limits?

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.690
I may not be Hanekawa-neesan,

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.730
but I'm an honor student, too.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:42.740
I can at least come up with an excuse
to get a teacher to lend me a key.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:45.490
What business did you have on the rooftop?

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:50.950
Once I entered Naoetsu High School,
I thought about my own safety.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.210
<b>STOP</b>

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.210
<b>STOP</b>

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.210
<i>She's a girl who's especially cautious of other people.</i>

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.000
<i>For a different reason than why Hanekawa checked out Naoetsu High School,</i>

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.560
<i>she said she thoroughly examined the grounds to see where it's safe or dangerous,</i>

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.860
<i>and to determine allies and foes.</i>

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.670
<i>And she found a bouquet on the off-limits rooftop,</i>

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:11.850
<i>so the story goes.</i>

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.830
An apparition story,

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.480
though it's not quite a ghost story,

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:16.980
but...

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.250
when you think about it, it's a rather strange tale, isn't it?

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.500
BLACK

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:22.790
<i>Yes.</i>

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.190
<i>It's a strange tale.</i>

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:27.380
<i>In the 18-year history of Naoetsu High School,</i>

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:31.870
<i>there hasn't been an incident where a student died.</i>

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:34.790
<b>...WELL, THAT ASIDE,</b>

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:34.830
<b>...WELL, THAT ASIDE,</b>

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:34.890
<b>...WELL, THAT ASIDE,</b>

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:34.950
<b>HOW AM I GOING TO GET INSIDE THE BUILDING.....?</b>

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:35.000
<b>HOW AM I GOING TO GET INSIDE THE BUILDING.....?</b>

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:35.890
<b>HOW AM I GOING TO GET INSIDE THE BUILDING.....?</b>

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.390
So, what do you think, Oshino?

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:43.550
Is the story I brought you worth anything close to 100,000 yen?

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.800
What?

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:52.680
Araragi-kun, do you know that girl's phone number or email address?

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.680
No, I didn't ask her.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.310
Then, can you tell her this:

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.920
"I regret to say it doesn't meet my expectations,

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.650
so please find some other means to pay your bill."

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:08.030
Can I at least hear why this story isn't even worth one yen?

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:13.270
First off, regarding the traffic accident site you guys saw,

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.540
there actually was a fatality a month ago.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.560
Oh, I see.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:24.000
That intersection's structure makes
traffic accidents common to begin with.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:26.490
I see.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:30.050
Well, Senjougahara almost jumped into the road, too.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.090
Oh, but in Senjougahara's case,

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:36.310
it was because she was distracted by the flowers put there as an offering.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:39.080
So it's not an issue of the road's structure.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.830
The problem is,

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.080
NOTHING

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.080
NOTHING

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.080
NOTHING

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.080
NOTHING

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:45.070
although no students had committed
suicide by jumping off the building,

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:48.570
and there weren't any accidents where someone fell,

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:49.820
for some reason,

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.570
there was a bouquet placed on every single rooftop,

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:53.840
correct?

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.830
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:00.470
Well, putting aside whether or not someone could actually fall,

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:04.190
rooftops are actually places where it's easy for an accident to occur.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:06.730
That's why they're off-limits.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.990
Well, schools that allow their students on the rooftops

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:14.490
surround the edge with ridiculously high fences.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.720
Right.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.530
So, roads, schools or wherever,

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:22.030
there are places where it's likely
that accidents and incidents will occur.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:23.480
In short,

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:26.250
it's like the opposite of a spot filled with positive energy?

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.960
You mean a spiritually bad spot?

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:32.490
Well, I think I've heard of that.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.700
Like facing in a direction that's bad luck.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.720
No, this is different from things like that.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:42.460
There are a multitude of places countrywide that are prone to accidents.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:46.830
Also, there are places people tend to choose to commit suicide.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:51.860
But those are problems of how the land is shaped,
or something else environmental.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.790
There's no connection to any spiritual elements.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.110
Senjougahara almost jumping into the street

00:07:57.110 --> 00:08:02.480
was a problem with the angle of the bouquet
and not anything like an apparition or spirit.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:04.010
Yeah.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:09.500
That's why I'm thinking about going to reposition that bouquet right now.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.080
Araragi-kun.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:15.510
If a bouquet placed in offering can cause an accident...

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.510
don't you think the opposite can happen as well?

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.010
<i>What you'd call an epilogue, or the punch line for this episode.</i>

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.850
<i>The punch line didn't come until much later.</i>

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:32.520
<i>Because I was satisfied by Oshino's explanation,</i>

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:35.360
<i>I forgot to brief Senjougahara about it.</i>

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:39.720
<i>I remembered it sometime in late May.</i>

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:40.240
BLACK

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.350
I just remembered.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:47.960
In short, those bouquets were a part of the school's rooftop access control.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:49.940
Access control?

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:50.910
Right.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.930
Just like managing keys or putting up fences.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.050
Well, compared to those two,

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:00.370
it's more like a reassurance, a good luck charm or a jinx.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:04.120
How is putting bouquets on rooftops
considered access control?

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.640
It's a rather tasteless ploy.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:11.780
By placing a bouquet, implying "someone died here,"

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:17.320
they wanted it to act as a warning that "this place is dangerous."

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.650
<b>DANGER
DO NOT
ENTER{not really readable but sure}</b>

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.030
Act as a warning?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.820
Like, "Accident-prone area ahead"?

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:27.110
Someone probably thought the ordinary
"Danger" sign wouldn't be effective enough.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.020
I mean, it's rather powerful,

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.040
the message that "someone died here in the past."

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:38.990
But is that any more effective than a jinx?

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:44.760
Well, Oshino said that it's like a reassurance, done in a playful manner.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.620
Things like fences and locking doors
should be enough to prevent people falling.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:52.720
But even then, it's not perfect.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:57.690
There are students who lie their way onto the rooftop, like you.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:09:59.510
Hold on, Araragi-kun.

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:02.570
You shouldn't call someone a liar.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:02.850
BLACK

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.990
I just have a glib tongue.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:06.710
You mean a sharp tongue!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.620
Glib and sharp are the worst!

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:17.920
So, in addition to the imperfect access control, the school has reassurance from a "charm."

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.340
I see.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.050
But I wonder how Oshino-san...

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:27.740
determined that just by listening to your story?

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:30.520
I can't say he "determined" it.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:34.310
See, you and I both had the same misunderstanding.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.550
Whether it's an accident or suicide,

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:39.180
if someone fell from the rooftop,

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.450
you wouldn't put the bouquet there.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.680
You'd put it on the ground where they fell.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.090
I see.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.590
So it was a misunderstanding.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:53.440
But it's also a mistake anyone could make.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.570
She's quick to justify her mistakes.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:11:00.840
Well, whoever did this, even if they realized the discrepancy,

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:04.090
had no choice but to put the bouquets on the rooftops.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.580
However.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:09.180
Such acts won't be committed from now on.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.020
<i>Right.</i>

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.480
<i>The fact that they started renovating the rooftops</i>

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:16.010
<i>was what made me remember this incident.</i>

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.360
<b>PRECONSTRUCTION</b>

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:20.980
<i>They were forced to renovate
the rooftops because there was a rumor</i>

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:27.100
<i>that "some student got on the roof
by climbing the side of the building."</i>

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:34.180
<i>The school never imagined someone would be
stupid enough to get on the rooftop from the exterior.</i>

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:37.060
<i>Installing a new fence is expensive.</i>

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:41.200
<i>So if they ever figure out I was that intruder,</i>

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.450
<i>it wouldn't end with just my expulsion.</i>

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:49.370
<i>Of course, for encouraging such an act,
Senjougahara may not go unpunished.</i>

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.370
Araragi-kun.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.280
I know.

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.650
This is a secret just between us.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.080
No.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.870
It's not enough to keep it a secret.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.630
Not enough? Then what do we do?

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:04.650
What we've done all this time, of course.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.570
All this time?

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.070
BLACK

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:10.060
We forget about it.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:37.980
<b>Nayami ketobashite ishi ga korogatte ku</b>

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:37.980
<b>Kicking a stone as if I was kicking my troubles</b>

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:43.740
<b>Sukoshi gomakashita are wa shigatsu no koto</b>

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:43.740
<b>It was April when I played my trick</b>

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:49.200
<b>Koukishin ousei de akarui kodomo deshita</b>

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:49.200
<b>I was a curious and cheerful child</b>

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:54.950
<b>Senaka oshita no wa ano hi kara no boku de</b>

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:54.950
<b>The me from the past gave me a push</b>

00:12:55.450 --> 00:13:00.840
<b>Hamidasenai retsu wo oinuite</b>

00:12:55.450 --> 00:13:00.840
<b>Let's loiter on the way</b>

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:06.420
<b>Michikusa wo shiyou</b>

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:06.420
<b>Passing a line you can't even lean out from</b>

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:14.070
<b>Kago ni nose taisetsu na yume</b>

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:14.070
<b>I'll put my precious dreams in the basket</b>

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:19.480
<b>pedaru mawashi tooku made saa mochi dasou</b>

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:19.480
<b>and spin the pedals, carrying them far away!</b>

